<title>UK: P. Duffryn 6.7 mln stg gain in stake sale.</title>
<headline>P. Duffryn 6.7 mln stg gain in stake sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British ports and engineering company Powell Duffryn said on Monday it had made a gain of 6.7 million stg by selling off its 50 percent shareholding in Corrall-Montenay Ltd to its joint venture partner.</p>
<p>The company said it had sold its stake in the energy management firm for 9.6 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>The 6.7 million stg gain will be included in the group's results for the year ending March 31, 1998, the company said.</p>
<p>The gain had been realised after charging goodwill of 1.3 million stg which was previously written off directly to reserves.</p>
